      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniontown%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1848, government agents Richard Cummins and Alfred Vaughan established a Potawatomi trading post that would become the town’s first site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kansashistory.gov/p/uniontown/12228"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town moved to its current location around 1865, roughly a decade after the post office opened east of the original spot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniontown%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A Missouri Pacific Railroad depot stood in Uniontown around 1900, marking the town’s role in regional rail transport.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
